HR4-POWER: discriminative power of  C(L) >= C(L/2)^2/C(0)   (zero MC, ~2 s)
========================================================================================================
[1] IDENTITY:  D := C(0)C(2t) - C(t)^2 = Var_nu(e^{-st}) >= 0   for every nu >= 0
========================================================================================================
  C(t) = int e^{-st} dnu(s)  =>  <e^{-st}>^2 <= <e^{-2st}>  (Cauchy-Schwarz in dnu)
  Symmetrised, the slack is a VARIANCE, i.e. it vanishes iff nu is a single atom.
  4000 random positive measures: D<0 in 0/4000 ;  max|D-Var|/C(0)^2 = 2.23e-16
  => 'satisfied' carries ZERO bits about the mass gap; a measured D<0 is an
     ESTIMATOR statement (bias or noise), never a statement about the model.  [T]

[1b] the estimator actually run on the data is the PERIODIC-time (finite Lt) one:
     C(t) = sum_n w_n [ e^{-m_n t} + e^{-m_n(Lt-t)} ].  Per mode, at argument 2t,
     slack = w_n b (1-a^2)^2 with a = e^{-m_n t}, b = e^{-m_n(Lt-2t)} , and b > 0 for
     every Lt  =>  D >= 0 for EVERY (Lt, L, nu).  Numeric check:
  3000 random (nu, Lt, t): D<0 in 0/3000  (max |D|/C(0)^2 = 2.34e+36)
  => on the actual Lt=12/16/20 data the SIGN of D is guaranteed by positivity;
     the inequality cannot be falsified by any model in the class.  [T]

